# No Phone Policy

**Website Announces "No Phone Policy"** (Also Known as the "No Phone Statement").

This policy primarily commits to the following points:

## No User Left Behind on Desktop

Our website will always be accessible via the desktop version, no matter what!

- Whether you're using a mobile browser or a desktop browser, users can fully access the site without being forced to use a mobile app.
- Users can browse the website using either a computer or mobile browser anytime, anywhere, with a consistent experience. There will be no restrictions based on the device used.

## No Phone? No Problem!

**No phone is required** to use the website at any time.

- There is no mandatory phone number registration; you can use an email or other methods to log in.  
   Your experience will not be affected or prevented just because you don't have a phone.
- Desktop and mobile users are treated equally, and those without a phone will not be discriminated against in terms of user experience.

## No Mandatory Phone Numbers

Phone numbers are private information, not tools for websites to harass users.

- Users can register, log in, and use the website without the need for a phone number.
- The website will never force users to provide or share phone numbers because we don’t need them!
- If additional verification is required for certain features, the website will provide alternative solutions, such as email verification or 2FA apps, and never require phone numbers.
